WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.168
Racquel: How can I see these guys

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.670
Racquel: on the inside as human beings?

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.587
♪

00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:05.797
Racquel: I can understand

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:08.216
Racquel: how you're just reduced to something that

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:08.925
was a mistake.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.095
Reggie: Life is not a straight line and it's a maze.

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:13.763
Orlando: There's a larger story at play

00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:15.140
Orlando: about resistance.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.475
Orlando: That's what the boys left us with. Right?

00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:18.476
Resist.

00:00:18.476 --> 00:00:23.690
♪

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.444
Reggie: One of our central questions is are we truly free

00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:30.697
Reggie: when our brothers and sisters are not free?

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.991
Character: What happens to a dream deferred?

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:36.202
Dr. John Carlos: There are more black people

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.037
in the penitentiaries across this nation

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.707
Dr. John Carlos: then there were black people enslaved

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.500
before the civil war.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.169
I've never done anything like this before.

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:46.713
Dr. John Carlos: So for me to walk in, man and digest

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.590
Dr. John Carlos: a script that they gave me,

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.592
Dr. John Carlos: was challenging for me.

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:53.094
I have this history or legacy. It's about humanity.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:54.429
Dr. John Carlos: When we came together

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:55.388
Dr. John Carlos: we could move a mountain.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:59.809
Reggie: This has been a unique treat because we bring

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:01.436
a lot of the incarcerated people

00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:02.520
Reggie: front and center.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.397
Reggie: We really, really get to meet them,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.982
Reggie:  just real life human beings.

00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:07.859
Our students are future scientists

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:09.819
and this semester they're working with bee colonies

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:11.529
and understanding how bees help the earth.

00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:11.988
♪

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:14.073
Reggie: I really just love like the idea of bees.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.034
Reggie: It's a really interesting juxtaposition of

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:18.203
Reggie: young black men in that environment.

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:21.039
Reggie:  You might say that they're dangerous and bad.

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:23.333
Reggie: But the planet needs them,

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:25.502
Reggie: they help the world be better.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:29.130
Racquel: Vince was a really great entry point to that

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.965
because they know him.

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:34.260
Racquel: You're not just an awful person,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.095
Racquel: you have layers. And that was really, really

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.431
Racquel: important for me to get through because

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.559
I even did a stint in jail when I was like their age.

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:43.770
Racquel: I'm very much into redemption

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.729
I mean, I am that.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:46.648
So there's no way I wouldn't want people

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:48.024
to see that in these characters.

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:51.152
You are not your biggest mistake.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.363
That really means something

00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:54.489
I'm glad

00:01:54.489 --> 00:02:00.537
♪

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:02.413
Reggie: The other amazing thing that happens

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:04.249
Reggie: is that they play a basketball game

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:07.335
Reggie: against a team comprised of these incarcerated

00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:09.796
Reggie: young men. As we started doing rehearsals,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.839
Reggie: I just kept saying but guys,

00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:13.591
Reggie: like what if we just do it all in one shot?

00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:16.928
John: Reggie was referencing that film on 1917,

00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:19.597
John: which is shot by one of the greatest DP's ever.

00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:21.641
John: I think they won the Oscar for that film.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.851
So I'm like, yeah, no, we'll do that.

00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:25.854
No problem, me? Oh, yeah. Easy.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:27.814
John: I already do camera workouts,

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:28.857
John: but the way he was describing it,

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:30.108
John: I'm like, I guess I just need to like

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:32.485
John: double my workouts for the next the month,

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.444
which I started doing.

00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:36.781
John: so we see it from the back. Yeah.

00:02:36.781 --> 00:02:38.408
So you're down there when that shot goes up.

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:39.492
Crew Member:  All the background

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.411
Crew Member:  go behind that tree over there please.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.331
Reggie: It was like 6 minutes of just holding a camera up.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.708
Reggie: And it was really, you know,

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:49.544
Reggie: technically just an amazing cinematic feat

00:02:49.544 --> 00:02:50.670
Reggie: that we were able to pull that off.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.297
♪

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:54.424
Reggie: As much as I like to say,

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:56.551
Reggie: this is not solely a basketball show,

00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:57.635
Reggie: basketball is important.

00:02:57.635 --> 00:02:59.470
Reggie: Really, love this idea of it

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.264
Reggie: have to get the audience at the edge of their seat

00:03:01.264 --> 00:03:02.265
Reggie: and while they're leaning forward

00:03:02.265 --> 00:03:02.849
Reggie: hit them with the truth.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:12.025
♪

